// idem_app -- the entry point of a game written the right way round.
//
// A game is `id`: it owns its state, its rules, its input and its drawing, and
// it imports the engine as a library. Its `.idml` lays out a screen over the top
// and decides nothing (docs/IDML.md). This is the loop that runs that
// arrangement, and it is deliberately thin -- everything interesting is on the
// game's side of six named functions:
//
//     g_init()            bring the game's state into existence
//     g_stage(k)          0 width, 1 height, 2 scale, 3 fps -- in the game's units
//     g_step(dt)          one frame of rules, dt in milliseconds
//     g_draw()            draw the world into the stage
//     g_ref(name)         what `@name` in the layout reads
//     g_act(name)         what a bare identifier in the layout calls
//
// There is no dynamic dispatch in `id` and none is wanted: g_ref and g_act are
// string compares over names the game itself chose, which is a short list, fixed
// at authoring time and worth writing down.
//
// **This directory is in the wrong place and knows it.** It belongs at
// engine/game/run/app/, and every directory on the way there already holds three
// entries -- the tree is saturated by the model this one replaces. It moves up
// when idem_boot and the interpreter under scr/ come out.
//
// Contrast idem_boot next door, which interprets a game *out of* a document.
// That is the model docs/IDML_GAME.md described and docs/IDML.md withdraws; it
// survives only until flappy and fps are converted, and then it goes.

idem_app(string[] chunks, int argc, string[] argv) {
  idem_init();
  idem_pre(argc, argv);
  idem_alay(run_join(chunks, 0, ""));
} return int idem_ago(argc, argv);

// The document is lexed and parsed for its *layout* -- definitions, variants and
// the `./` page -- and nothing is looked for in it beyond that. Then the game is
// brought up and the window opened at the size the game asks for.
idem_alay(string src) {
  scn_root(src, 0);
  ui_pinit();
  idem_alay1(src);
} return void;

idem_alay1(string src) {
  lex_init();
  idem_alay2(src);
} return void;
